# (0.23) Edit: Atari line ends and File > Print (text shell). The card copy gets
# tests/editp.lst as /PROG.LST: Atari line ends ($9B), an inverse word ($C8 $C5 ...).
# Edit shows its lines, the status line says "Atari line ends" (shot 1); a line typed at
# the top, ctrl-S (saved with $9B line ends again, the inverse word cleared: compared with
# tests/editp-lst.txt), ctrl-P: "Printed" on the status line (shot 2); the job
# /Printouts/2026-01-01 00.00.00 Edit.txt has LF line ends (tests/editp-job1.txt). Then
# ctrl-N, two lines typed (the last one without a line end), F10: File open with Print
# (shot 3), Print chosen from the keyboard: the job "... Edit 2.txt" (tests/editp-job2.txt:
# a line end after the last line).
1500 {esc}
+1500 edit PROG.LST\n
# shot 1 at 5.0 s
5500 5 REM PRINTED\n
7000 {dE0}s{uE0}
7500 {dE0}p{uE0}
# shot 2 at 8.5 s
9000 {dE0}n{uE0}
9500 Dear printer,\nthis line came from Edit.
12500 {d43}{u43}
# shot 3 at 13.5 s: File open; Down x4: New, Open, Save, Save as, Print (separator skipped)
14000 {down}{down}{down}{down}
+500 \n
# shot 4 at 16.0 s: "Printed"
